    {
      "id": 361536,
      "username": "JNJH",
      "name": "JH",
      "created_at": "2023-04-27T15:43:13.460Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Thanks, Patrick.</p>\n<p>While you’re looking at the email code…I also posted these 2 issues but got no response at the time.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"99888\">\n  <div class=\"title\">\n    <div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n    <img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/4af34b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\">\n    <a href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/t/email-initial-sync-count-ignored/99888\">Email Initial Sync Count ignored?</a> <a class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/erpnext/6\"><span data-category-id=\"6\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #BF1E2E; --category-badge-text-color: #FFFFFF;\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category \"><span class=\"badge-category__name\">ERPNext</span></span></a>\n  </div>\n  <blockquote>\n    I have connected my email account. I set \nEmail Sync Option = ALL \nInitial Sync Count = 250 \nSo far it has ingested 11,312 of my old emails and it’s still running… \nWhy is Initial Sync Count not respected? \nCan I cancel the sync process? Because it is still ingesting emails from 7 years ago and may end uo with hundreds of thousands that I don’t need.\n  </blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>\nI think the most user friendly option would actually be to allow the user to specify a starting date for initial ingestion (rather than a count of emails), for example when migrating from another system.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"99896\">\n  <div class=\"title\">\n    <div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n    <img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/4af34b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\">\n    <a href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/t/synced-inbound-emails-shows-in-timelin-with-ingested-date-time-not-the-email-date-time/99896\">Synced inbound emails shows in timelin with ingested date/time not the email date/time</a> <a class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/erpnext/6\"><span data-category-id=\"6\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #BF1E2E; --category-badge-text-color: #FFFFFF;\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category \"><span class=\"badge-category__name\">ERPNext</span></span></a>\n  </div>\n  <blockquote>\n    It’s great that in a Contact timeline you can see related historical emails with no intervention, but on the timeline these emails show with the ingested date/time not the email date/time. And the original date sent is not shown in the header in timeline view so there is no way of knowing what the original date was. The emails are in Communication Inbox with the correct date/times. \nIs it possible to customise this behaviour?\n  </blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>\nSimilarly I think when migrating from another system, constructing an historical timeline would be beneficial.</p>",
